  "result": "Excellent! All 184 tests pass. I've successfully added credit notes functionality:\n\n\u2705 **Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code** to src/errors.js\n\n\u2705 **Created src/credits.js** with `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`:\n\n**Validation:**\n- Status must be 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (error: NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n- Amount must be positive integer (error: AMOUNT_INVALID)\n- Amount cannot exceed invoice total (error: CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n\n**Returns** `ok(creditNote)` with:\n- `number`: Credit note number (CN-YYYY-CCCC format, separate counter from invoices)\n- `invoiceNumber`: The invoice's number\n- `customerId`: Customer ID\n- `amount`: Credit amount\n- `reason`: Reason for credit\n- `date`: Credit note issue date\n\n**Numbering:**\n- Format: `CN-YYYY-CCCC` (CN prefix, year, 4-digit counter)\n- Separate counter from invoices (both INV and CN can be in existingNumbers)\n- Counter resets each year\n- Sequential within each year\n\n\u2705 **14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Creating credits for issued/partially_paid/paid invoices\n- NOT_ISSUED protection (prevents credits on drafts)\n- AMOUNT_INVALID for invalid amounts (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- CREDIT_TOO_HIGH for excessive amounts\n- Sequential credit note numbering\n- Year-based counter separation\n- Mixed invoice and credit note numbers\n- Edge cases (invoices without numbers, partial/full credits)\n\nCredit notes are now fully implemented with proper validation, numbering, and support for refunds on any issued invoice state.",
